WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:03.636
PEGGY SCOTT:
<i> It's from the publisher
 of</i> The Christian Advocate.

00:00:03.636 --> 00:00:04.637
Why is he writing you?

00:00:05.237 --> 00:00:06.473
He wants to meet.

00:00:08.073 --> 00:00:09.942
Are you enjoying
your stay in New York?

00:00:10.242 --> 00:00:11.577
I'd love to tell you
all about it.

00:00:11.677 --> 00:00:12.345
<i> Who'd object to that?</i>

00:00:12.779 --> 00:00:15.081
Oh, Henry, Henry,
must you live on in your child?

00:00:15.148 --> 00:00:17.249
Can you not set her free
for pity's sake?

00:00:18.284 --> 00:00:23.422
Having a new rail station
in this city isn't as popular
as we'd hoped it might be.

00:00:23.456 --> 00:00:24.491
(CHUCKLING)

00:00:25.424 --> 00:00:26.792
BERTHA RUSSELL:
<i> Mrs. Morris is leaving.</i>

00:00:27.326 --> 00:00:28.761
GEORGE RUSSELL:<i> I thought
 you were honorable men.</i>

00:00:28.928 --> 00:00:31.598
Not too honorable
to miss the chance
of a fast buck, of course.

00:00:31.698 --> 00:00:33.032
But not greedy, dirty thieves!

00:00:33.099 --> 00:00:34.000
Mr. Russell...

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:36.301
GEORGE:<i> Would you have tried
 to get the better of me?</i>

00:00:36.602 --> 00:00:39.606
<i> How could I allow that
 to go unpunished?</i>

